   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "population": "cordon",
   "story": "Northfork canned beans and river fish for forty years. In the second week the Cordon took it over to pack rations for the evacuation: the night shift kept the retorts going under guard, the trucks backed up to the dock every morning, and a quartermaster held the cold-store key and counted every case out. When the Bloom got into the line the guards chained the front office and left the shift on the floor. The quartermaster locked herself in the cold store with the stock. The foreman hung the spare key in his office on the gallery and wrote the last entry in the tally book.",
